{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.LogSineSingularPart","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.LogSineSingularPart","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Integrals.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Knot.LogFactorialStirling"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_cell_telescope","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_cell_telescope","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSingularPart.lean#L73-L120","doc":"**L4-1c(i) — the singular part telescopes exactly (sorry-free).**  For\nevery grid spacing `h > 0` and every `n`,\n\n    Σ_{j=1}^{n} ( ∫_{(j−1)h}^{jh} log u du − h·log(jh) )\n      = h · ( n·log n − n − log(n!) ).\n\nThe `log h` pieces cancel identically and the `log j` pieces telescope;\nthe right-hand side is exactly the combination the Stirling brick\n(`tendsto_log_factorial_stirling`) evaluates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.integral_log_cell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.integral_log_cell","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/LogSineSingularPart.lean#L63-L71","doc":"The per-cell primitive difference, from Mathlib's hypothesis-free\n`integral_log` (which covers the first cell `[0, h]` through the\nsingularity, `log 0 = 0` making the boundary term vanish). ","signatureChunk":0}]}